  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "The researchers developed SnapScope, an open-source platform for harvesting and analyzing public, geotagged Snapchat stories at a city scale. They tested the system in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia, collecting 515,364 unique snaps over 23 days using a 1 km grid of 2,740 query points, with a saturation probe showing that 94.8% of returned records in consecutive runs were duplicates.",
      "why": "It provides a reproducible, city-agnostic pipeline and interactive interface to collect and explore ephemeral social media data that was previously inaccessible due to the lack of a documented API."
